📝 Project Summary: IoT Temperature & Humidity Monitor
🔧 Hardware
ESP8266 + DHT11 Sensor

Reads temperature and humidity every 60 seconds

Sends data to your Flask API over HTTP using JSON

🌐 Backend (Hosted on EC2)
Flask API with SQLite

/api/data: Accepts sensor data via POST

/api/latest: Returns the most recent reading

/api/history: Returns the last N readings (used in the graph)

Database

SQLite stores each reading with timestamp, temperature, and humidity

API Key Authentication

X-API-KEY header added to secure /api/data route

Unauthorized requests are rejected with 401

📊 Frontend Dashboard
HTML page with:

Live temperature & humidity readings

Real-time chart (Chart.js) showing historical data (last 50 entries)

🚨 Alerting
Telegram Bot Integration

Sends alert if temperature > 30°C or humidity < 25%

Email Alerts

Sends an email with current values when the same conditions are met

🔐 Secret Management
.env file used for:

Telegram token, email credentials, API key, etc.

Used python-dotenv to load secrets into Flask app

.env added to .gitignore to prevent accidental leaks

